contumacy. Accent the first syllable; see RECESSIVE ACCENT.
===
**contumacy.** Accent the first syllable; see ^^RECESSIVE ACCENT^^.
>>>

<<<
contumely. The possible pronunciations, given here in order of merit, are no less than five:— ko’ntimli, ké’ntimé’li, k6/ntamily, konti’mili, konti’mli.
===
**contumely.** The possible pronunciations, given here in order of merit, are no less than five:—kŏ'ntūmlĭ, kŏ'ntūmē'lĭ, kŏ'ntūmĭlĭ, kontū'mĭlĭ, kontū'mlĭ.
>>>

<<<
The wellknown line The oppressor’s wrong, the proud man’s c. does much to kill
===
The well-known line *The oppressor's wrong, the proud man's c.* does much to kill
>>>

<<<
which seems to those whose | knowledge of metre is limited to fit blank verse better than the second & third.
===
which seems to those whose knowledge of metre is limited to fit blank verse better than the second & third.
>>>

<<<
The second is kept in being by contumelious.
===
The second is kept in being by *contumelious*.
>>>

